WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.263
Hi everyone! I am Luca, from LucaLampariello.com

00:00:03.263 --> 00:00:09.886
and today, I'd like to make a video in Greek..finally!

00:00:09.994 --> 00:00:15.594
I'd like to tell you how and why I started learning Greek.

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:24.417
I visited Greece for the first time some twenty years ago

00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:30.411
and spent two weeks in these two small islands: Paxos-Antipaxos.

00:00:30.411 --> 00:00:37.441
And of course, the beaches were beautiful and the sea was crystaline.

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:45.158
It is a renowned fact that in Greece, especially in the summer, the weather is beautiful

00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:59.994
but it is not only that the weather is beautiful, but the people (guys and most of all girls) are very nice.

00:00:59.994 --> 00:01:07.128
I know that this might sound like a stereotype, but this has been my personal experience in Greece.

00:01:07.128 --> 00:01:20.247
Greeks laugh a lot, they gesticulate a lot, speak loud, and are often in a good mood.

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:32.246
I like thinking that the Greek language sounds like Spanish but has an Italian heart.

00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:40.731
A few years later, I went back to Greece, to Corfu

00:01:40.731 --> 00:01:46.947
and finally, three years ago, I went to Thessanolink for the Polyglot Conference.

00:01:46.947 --> 00:01:58.717
When I was in Thessaloniki, at a certain point, I told myself "I am sure now that I am going to learn Greek"

00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:08.517
At that time, I was learning other languages, so. I decided I would start learning Greek a bit later.

00:02:08.517 --> 00:02:18.833
Finally, I started learning Greek in September 2017

00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:27.734
Now, how did I actually start learning Greek?

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:35.603
At the beginning, as I always do with European languages, I used a book which is called ASSIMIL.

00:02:35.603 --> 00:02:44.336
For all those who don't know the ASSIMIL system, it is a bilingual book

00:02:44.336 --> 00:02:54.336
wihch has one page in Greek, and on the other page Italian, my native language.

00:02:54.336 --> 00:03:03.867
I translate from Greek into Italian, and then from Italian into Greek.

00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:12.688
Unfortunately, I don't have time to explain things in details how this method works,

00:03:12.688 --> 00:03:24.621
but let me tell you that this methodology allows me to acquire the foundation of any language.

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:35.323
After I finished ASSIMIL, I started working on a language series which is called Pod101, and I did it for a few months.

00:03:35.323 --> 00:03:46.137
I found a series which the American University offers for free on the internet.

00:03:46.137 --> 00:03:49.666
You can find the link in the description box.

00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:55.577
It is a very interesting series, which I really loved

00:03:55.577 --> 00:04:03.078
but the truth is, I started having a lot of fun

00:04:03.078 --> 00:04:08.543
when I started using authentic material.

00:04:08.543 --> 00:04:13.775
For example, ASTRONIO is a YouTube channel about the Universe,

00:04:13.775 --> 00:04:20.241
about astronomy, and those videos are really great!

00:04:20.241 --> 00:04:24.512
At the beginning it was a bit difficult to understand the content,

00:04:24.512 --> 00:04:29.076
because the presenter spoke very fast.

00:04:29.076 --> 00:04:33.595
With time though, I started understanding more and more.

00:04:33.595 --> 00:04:40.626
I started watching other channels, for example, Easy Greek.

00:04:40.626 --> 00:04:44.026
As wth Astronio, at the beginning it seemed to me that

00:04:44.026 --> 00:04:48.877
people spoke very fast, but now I understand a lot

00:04:48.877 --> 00:04:51.494
because I got used to it.

00:04:51.494 --> 00:04:59.027
Of course, I understand these videos because they have subtitles,

00:04:59.027 --> 00:05:03.211
without them it would be quite difficult to understand.

00:05:03.211 --> 00:05:09.185
For this reason, I try to find material with subtitles.

00:05:12.575 --> 00:05:15.879
Now, how did I learn to SPEAK Greek?

00:05:15.879 --> 00:05:18.647
I started last year in July

00:05:18.647 --> 00:05:27.698
when I started to talk with a fantastic girl, a fantastic Greek girl who goes by the name of Daria.

00:05:27.698 --> 00:05:36.048
Daria is a teacher on ITALKI - you can find her profile in the description box

00:05:36.393 --> 00:05:46.683
I started chatting with her in Greek and we talked for 30 minutes, twice a week.

00:05:46.683 --> 00:05:53.990
But only now have we started speaking twice a week.

00:05:54.069 --> 00:05:55.242
To wrap up,

00:05:55.292 --> 00:05:59.666
in the case of Greek, I knew exactly what I wanted.

00:05:59.666 --> 00:06:10.083
First, it is important that you know exactly why you have started and why you want to learn a given language.

00:06:10.083 --> 00:06:17.368
Second, it is important that you choose the right resources from the very beginning.

00:06:17.368 --> 00:06:26.400
Third, it is important that you speak with someone who is nice, and that you speak about interesting things.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.238
Unfortunately, this is the end of the video.

00:06:30.238 --> 00:06:36.084
As always, I have written an extensive article about how I have learned Gree.

00:06:36.084 --> 00:06:45.035
Thanks a bunch to everyone and see you in the next videos!

